    "narrative": "The Austin Waves\u2019 offensive outlook for August 26th is anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** and **Kyle Tucker**, who represent our highest-ceiling plays at 80.76 and 77.97, respectively. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from an elite combination of a favorable matchup against McGreevy (4.47 xERA) and a 14% boost from platoon dynamics, while **Kyle Tucker** faces a vulnerable Smith-Shawver (5.23 xERA), providing the ideal environment to chase counting stats. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (77.71) and **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) round out the core, with both taking advantage of significant SP skill edges that elevate them well into the \"Strong\" start tier.\n\nTactically, we are leaning heavily into speed-skewed upside to combat the scarcity in the SB category. **Nasim Nunez** (56.21) remains in the lineup despite his #8 hole because his matchup against Gordon, T carries a 4% boost due to the pitcher\u2019s slow delivery, a niche edge we prioritize for theft opportunities. Conversely, **Luis Robert Jr.** (44.43) is the most marginal start of the day; his base projection is solid, but a severe 15% platoon penalty against May forces him to the bottom of our rankings. **Tommy White** (55.97) holds the UTIL spot over other bench options primarily due to a 10% park factor bump, though he faces a tougher test against Prielipp (3.96 xERA). \n\nRegarding roster management, **Heliot Ramos** was the most difficult exclusion from today\u2019s lineup; he fell just outside the threshold for active consideration due to his status as a non-starter. We continue to monitor the IR for **Andy Pages**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Jacob Wilson**, whose absences leave us thinner than ideal. We have opted to keep depth pieces like **Josh Jung**, **Coby Mayo**, **Curtis Mead**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Dominic Smith**, and **Wade Meckler** on the bench today, as their current projections fail to surpass the established floors of our primary starters. No major weather risks are flagged, but managers should note that while **Miguel Vargas** receives a 5% boost from wind-out conditions, he remains a high-variance start against Gore.",
